# Missing Value Handling Alignment, Imputation Benchmarking & Responsive UI Plan

## Executive Summary
This implementation plan addresses the feedback provided by petrophysical stakeholders and interviewers regarding missing value handling in **WellQC+**. It aligns system capabilities with domain-specific missing value diagnostics, introduces an evidence-based multi-method imputation benchmarking suite (KNN, Linear, Mean/Median, Spline, Row Dropping), and enhances responsive layout design across Mobile, Tablet, and Desktop viewports.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Stakeholder Alignment Highlights:**
> 1. **Root Cause Analysis (Why Data is Missing):** Automatically categorizes missing points by logging conditions (e.g., Casing Shoe boundaries, Borehole Washout, Sensor Telemetry Dropout, Off-Bottom intervals).
> 2. **Multi-Method Imputation Benchmarking:** Benchmarks Linear Interpolation baseline against **K-Nearest Neighbours (KNN)**, **Mean/Median**, **Spline**, and **Row Dropping** using RMSE, MAE, and R² validation scores.
> 3. **Threshold-Based Listwise Deletion:** Provides configurable thresholds (e.g. drop rows if missing % < 2%) to prevent unnecessary synthetic data generation when missingness is trivial.
> 4. **LAS Null Indicator Parsing:** Handles standard (`-999.25`, `-9999`) and custom header null representations defined in the `~Well` section.
> 5. **Full Mobile & Tablet Responsiveness:** Adds slide-out mobile navigation drawer, fluid grid layouts, and scrollable data tables for seamless access on smartphones, iPads/tablets, and desktop screens.

